# Test pairing allow list.
# Every entry must have a # [category] comment above its group.
# Entries without a category tag will fail the check.
#
# Regenerate: go tool devtools testpair update
#
# Categories:
#   [multi-file]  subcommand files tested via main_test.go
#   [cross-pkg]  test covers symbols from a different package
#   [convention]  naming follows project convention, not strict Go idiom
#   [scenario]  integration/scenario test not tied to one symbol

# [convention]
# assertOwnerOnly answers "may anything but the owner reach this path". That
# needs an access list on Windows and a mode everywhere else, so the helper
# splits by build tag. Its callers in load_test.go do not split:
# TestSave_RestrictsTheFileToItsOwner and TestInit_RestrictsTheFileToItsOwner.
# The code it checks lives in internal/fsretry, because the package performing
# a write is the one that owns what the file ends up readable by. Neither file
# has a source file to pair with, and an empty perm_other.go would exist for
# the pairing rule alone.
orphan-test internal/config/perm_other_test.go no source file internal/config/perm_other.go
orphan-test internal/config/perm_windows_test.go no source file internal/config/perm_windows.go

# [convention]
# TestHelperProcess is the standard library's idiom for testing code that
# spawns a subprocess. The test binary re-invokes itself and stands in for the
# external program. The pattern fixes the name, which matches no symbol
# because this is a process entrypoint rather than a test of one.
name-mismatch internal/deps/deps_test.go TestHelperProcess: no symbol 'HelperProcess' in package
name-mismatch internal/post/post_test.go TestHelperProcess: no symbol 'HelperProcess' in package
name-mismatch internal/procgroup/procgroup_test.go TestHelperProcess: no symbol 'HelperProcess' in package
name-mismatch internal/record/streamlink_test.go TestHelperProcess: no symbol 'HelperProcess' in package
name-mismatch internal/service/service_test.go TestHelperProcess: no symbol 'HelperProcess' in package
name-mismatch internal/fetch/fetch_test.go TestHelperProcess: no symbol 'HelperProcess' in package

# [scenario]
# The only test that registers a real task, behind //go:build schedulertest so
# it never runs in the suite. It drives comScheduler end to end rather than any
# symbol of its own, and a source file under the same tag would exist for the
# pairing rule alone. Run it by hand:
#   go test -tags schedulertest ./internal/service/
orphan-test internal/service/scheduler_live_windows_test.go no source file internal/service/scheduler_live_windows.go
